  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A plane which containing the line</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>This plane is perpendicular to the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;then</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Equation of plane is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math></p><p>Clearly,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> lies on the plane.</p>",
